\subsection{Test 1: graphs on 1,000 vertices}\label{sec:1000}


Perhaps one of the most important test results for us, as anticipated by Theorem~\ref{th:SBM-happy}, is verifying that if $k$ and $\rho$ are small enough, then communities of networks in the SBM induce a $\rho$-happy colouring. The results of the first test fully supports this, see Figure~\ref{fig:k-r-happy}. On the other hand, when $k$ or $\rho$ increases, the induced colouring by graph communities cannot make all the vertices $\rho$-happy. Especially when $\rho=1$, the induced colouring makes almost no vertex happy. 

